1	/**
2	 * Characterization tests for the shared date-filter module (RF-02).
3	 *
4	 * These lock the date-filter glue that is currently copy-pasted across the four
5	 * list pages — `expenses`, `receipts`, `transactions`, `reconciliation` — BEFORE
6	 * it is extracted into `$lib/utils/sharedDateFilter`. They are written against the
7	 * module's contract, not against inline reimplementations, so they actually bind
8	 * to the extracted unit (unlike the previous version of this file, which tested
9	 * private copies of the logic and gave false confidence).
10	 *
11	 * Repo convention (see the other *-page-filters specs): pure logic is unit-tested
12	 * in the node project; the reactive/`goto` wiring on each page is covered by
13	 * Playwright e2e. This file therefore targets the pure, extractable functions the
14	 * shared composable will delegate to.
15	 *
16	 * Specifications covered:
17	 * - #{#sdf1a} URL Query Parameter Date Filters
18	 * - #{#sdf1b} Automatic Filter Application from URL (client-side predicate)
19	 * - #{#sdf2a} URL Update Logic (apply / clear)
20	 * - #{#sdf5a} URL Parameter Validation
21	 *
22	 * RED PHASE: `$lib/utils/sharedDateFilter` does not exist yet — every test here
23	 * fails at import until RF-02 creates the module. That is intentional: it is the
24	 * red safety net that drives the extraction.
25	 */
